# =============================================================================
# sandbox.ogs - a city with wealth, services and a budget, explained line by
# line.
#
# This file is a ruleset. It holds no map and no building: it says what a
# building *is*, what it can hold, and what it does. The map lives next to it,
# in sandbox.ogc. Open one and you get the other.
#
# Read this file from top to bottom. Each block is explained before it starts.
#
# HOW TO READ THE SYNTAX
#
#   - A block has a name and is closed by the word "end".
#   - A "#" starts a comment. The rest of the line is ignored.
#   - Words are bare: no quotes, no commas, no semicolon.
#   - The order of the blocks does not matter to the engine. The order here is
#     the order that is easiest to read.
#   - Names are yours to choose. "People" and "Home" mean nothing to the
#     engine; it only checks that the same word is used everywhere.
#
# WHAT THE CITY DOES, IN ONE PARAGRAPH
#
#   Houses hold people. In the morning they send them to the factories and to
#   the shops, which turn people into goods, into money and into pollution.
#   Trucks carry the goods. The city collects a tax on every building and pays
#   for its services with it. Pollution, noise, crime and traffic reduce the
#   value of an address; parks, schools and public transport raise it. A
#   valuable address becomes a richer building, a bad one becomes a poorer one,
#   and in the end an empty one. Rich houses send their children to the
#   university, the university raises the skills of the district, and a district
#   with enough skills turns its factories into technology campuses.
#
# THE THREE IDEAS THIS FILE IS BUILT ON
#
#   1. WEALTH AND DENSITY ARE TWO DIFFERENT THINGS. Density comes from the zone
#      the player paints: a low zone grows small buildings, a high zone grows
#      tall ones. Wealth comes from an upgrade: every zone starts with its
#      poorest building and improves it, or ruins it, according to the ground
#      around it. Three densities times three levels of wealth gives the nine
#      residential types and the nine commercial types below.
#
#   2. THE TREASURY AND THE BUDGET ARE TWO DIFFERENT THINGS. "Money" is what
#      the city owns. "PoliceBudget" is the share the player grants to the
#      police. A rich city that grants nothing has no patrol at all. See the
#      section on the budget.
#
#   3. EVERY SYSTEM IS A CLOSED LOOP. A cause, an effect, and a way back to the
#      cause. Pollution reduces the value of the land, a low value ruins the
#      houses, and fewer houses produce less pollution. A system with no way
#      back is a number on a screen, not a game.
#
# IF YOU EDIT THIS FILE
#
#   A save records a fingerprint of the ruleset it was written against, and
#   refuses to open against a ruleset that changed since. Use Apply in the
#   Script panel of the demo: it reloads the rules and stamps the saves next
#   to this file with the new fingerprint.
# =============================================================================


# =============================================================================
# RESOURCES - the quantities the city counts.
#
# A resource is only a name. Nothing here says who holds it or how much.
# Everything below refers to these names, so this block comes first.
#
# There is one resource per counted quantity, whatever holds it. Three kinds of
# owner appear in the rules:
#
#   layer X    a number in one cell of the map. The ground.
#   local X    a number inside one building. Its stock.
#   global X   a number for the whole city. Its accounts.
#
# The same name may serve two owners: "Trash" is both a stock inside a shop and
# a number on the street outside it, and the two mean different things. The
# rules say which one they read.
# =============================================================================
resources
	# The ground: what the utilities supply and what the buildings foul.
	resource Water
	resource Grass
	resource Power
	resource Sewage
	resource Trash
	resource Pollution
	resource GroundPollution
	resource Noise
	resource Crime
	resource FireHazard
	resource Traffic

	# The ground again: what makes an address good or bad.
	resource Education
	resource Skills
	resource Health
	resource LandValue
	resource Desirability
	resource TransitCoverage
	resource Parks
	resource Tourism
	resource JobAccess
	resource Shopping

	# What a building holds.
	resource People
	resource Goods
	resource Food
	resource Ore
	resource Oil
	resource Happiness

	# What the city holds. Money is the treasury. The three demands are the
	# appetite of the city for new buildings. Jobs and Workers are the two
	# sides of the labour market. Graduates is what the university produces.
	resource Money
	resource ResidentialDemand
	resource CommercialDemand
	resource IndustrialDemand
	resource Jobs
	resource Workers
	resource Graduates

	# What the player grants. These are settings, not stocks: no rule ever
	# writes them, and the Budget panel of the demo is their only author. A
	# budget is a percentage from 0 to 100. A tax is a rate from 0 to 20.
	resource PoliceBudget
	resource FireBudget
	resource HealthBudget
	resource EducationBudget
	resource TransitBudget
	resource WasteBudget
	resource TaxResidential
	resource TaxCommercial
	resource TaxIndustrial
end


# =============================================================================
# PATHS AND SEGMENTS - the network the agents travel on.
#
# A "path" is a family of networks: roads here, but rails or water pipes would
# be other paths. Two paths never meet, so an agent that starts on a road stays
# on the road.
#
# A road drawn over another is cut, and the two meet at a crossroads a driver
# can turn at. That is what "crossings" says, and it is true unless you write
# otherwise. Add "crossings false" on a network of pipes or cables, where one
# line passing over another means nothing, and put the junctions you do want
# there by hand with the Nodes tool.
#
# A "segment" is one kind of connection between two crossroads:
#
#   speed      how fast an agent travels on it when it is empty.
#   capacity   how much traffic it takes before it slows down.
#   beta       how sharply it slows down once it is above that capacity.
#
# These three numbers are what the router uses to choose an itinerary. It does
# not look for the shortest road, but for the fastest one *now*: a short busy
# street can cost more than a long empty one.
# =============================================================================
paths
	path Road color 0xAAAAAA
end

segments
	segment Dirt color 0xAAAAAA speed 30 capacity 20 beta 4
	segment Avenue color 0xCCCCCC speed 50 capacity 60 beta 4
end


# =============================================================================
# AGENTS - who travels, and how fast.
#
# An agent is sent by a building, with a load of resources. It looks for a
# building that answers to the name it was given, goes there, and gives the
# load away. Then it disappears.
#
# The engine does not know what a "Worker" is. The agents below differ only by
# their colour and their speed. What makes one a worker and another a truck is
# the rule that sends it and the load it carries.
#
# AN AGENT LOOKS FOR A NAME, NOT FOR A TYPE. "agent Worker to Home" ends its
# trip in any building whose "targets" hold the word "Home". None of the nine
# houses below is called Home, and all nine answer to it. This is what lets a
# district improve its houses without breaking a single trip.
# =============================================================================
agents
	agent People color 0xFFFF00 speed 10
	agent Worker color 0xFFFFFF speed 10
	agent Shopper color 0xFFAA00 speed 12
	agent Diner color 0xFF6644 speed 12
	agent Truck color 0x8888FF speed 8
	agent GarbageTruck color 0x556B2F speed 6
	agent Student color 0x66CCFF speed 10
	agent Patient color 0xFF99AA speed 14
	agent Tourist color 0xFF66FF speed 9
end


# =============================================================================
# RULES - everything the city does.
#
# This is the long block, and the interesting one. A rule is a list of
# conditions and of changes, all on the same footing.
#
# THE ONE THING TO REMEMBER: a rule is all or nothing. The engine reads every
# line first. If a single one refuses, nothing happens at all, and the rule is
# tried again later. So a house cannot send a worker it does not have, and a
# shop cannot sell goods it never received.
#
# There are three kinds of rule, and each one runs on a different thing:
#
#   buildingRule   runs on one building.
#   layerRule      runs on the cells of one layer.
#   zoneRule       runs on one rectangle painted by the player.
#
# A rule written here does nothing yet. It has to be listed in the "rules [ ]"
# of a building, of a layer or of a zone, further down the file. That is what
# attaches it to something.
#
# THE LINES YOU WILL SEE
#
#   rate 30 minutes        how often the rule is tried. Game time, not real
#                          time. A bare number would count engine ticks, and
#                          twenty ticks make one game minute, which says
#                          nothing to a reader. Write the unit on the same
#                          line as the number.
#
#   hour between 8 18      only between 8:00 and 18:00 on the city clock. If
#                          the first hour is the larger one, the range crosses
#                          midnight: "hour between 21 3" is the night.
#
#   local People greater 0    a condition on the stock of *this* building.
#   local People remove 1     take one from it.
#   global Money add 1        the treasury of the whole city.
#   layer Pollution add 1     the ground around the building. How far around
#                             is the "layerRadius" of the building.
#
#   agent Worker to Work add [ People 1 ]
#                          send a Worker carrying one People, looking for a
#                          building that answers to the name "Work".
#
#   onFail OtherRule       when this rule refuses, try that one instead. This
#                          is how a graded effect is written. See the budget.
#
# Note that "add" and "remove" are changes, while "greater" and "less" are
# conditions. Both are checked before anything runs.
#
# TWO PRECISE POINTS, BECAUSE THEY DECIDE THE NUMBERS BELOW
#
#   "greater" and "less" are strict. "greater 0" means one or more.
#
#   "add" refuses when the target is already full. A rule that ends with
#   "layer Pollution add 1" stops entirely once the ground around the building
#   holds as much as it can. This is why production and pollution are two
#   separate rules here: a saturated street must not close the factory.
#
# HOW A BUILDING WRITES ON A LAYER, AND WHY THE NUMBERS ARE LARGE
#
#   "layerRadius 4" is a diamond of 41 cells around the building. When a rule
#   writes "layer Water add 400", the engine hands the 400 out cell by cell, in
#   random order, filling each cell to the capacity of the layer before it moves
#   to the next one. It does not give 400 to every cell, and it does not give
#   ten to each.
#
#   So a supply is a flow, and the capacity of the layer is the size of one
#   cell. Water holds 20 per cell, and a tower supplies 400 per hour, which
#   fills twenty cells an hour: a diamond of 41 cells is served in about two
#   hours, and the tower then keeps the cells it already filled topped up.
#
#   READING IS A SUM OVER THE SAME DIAMOND. "layer Crime greater 25" inside a
#   building rule adds up the 41 cells and compares the total, not each cell.
#   So a threshold on a building is a threshold on a whole district, and it has
#   to be read against the reach of that building: the same figure means
#   something stricter on a police station of radius 4 than on a shop of
#   radius 1. The same holds for a change: "layer Crime remove 6" refuses
#   unless the district holds six between all its cells.
#
#   A zone rule is the exception, and reads one cell: see the note there.
# =============================================================================
rules

	# =========================================================================
	# 1. THE GROUND
	#
	# Two mechanisms write on a layer, and they are not the same.
	#
	# A layerRule is a rule: it runs on one cell at a time, reads that cell and
	# writes that cell. It expresses a threshold, such as "where the air is
	# dirty, the fire risk grows".
	#
	# Diffusion and decay are properties of the layer itself, declared in the
	# "layers" block far below. They express transport: smoke travels to the
	# streets nearby and fades in the air. A rule cannot say this, because a
	# rule never reads a cell other than its own. This is why Pollution, Noise,
	# Crime and the others carry "diffusion" and "decay" instead of a pair of
	# rules that add one and remove one.
	# =========================================================================

	# Water slowly becomes grass. The interesting word is randomTilesPercent:
	# the rule visits only one cell in ten, drawn at random, instead of every
	# cell. Over time the result is the same as visiting all of them, and it
	# costs less on a large map. It also looks better: the grass does not appear
	# everywhere at once.
	layerRule CreateGrass
		rate 20 minutes
		layer Water remove 1 randomTilesPercent 10
		layer Grass add 1
	end

	# Sewage that no treatment plant removes seeps into the ground. The
	# ground keeps it: GroundPollution decays once a day, not once an hour.
	layerRule SewageFoulsGround
		rate 2 hours
		layer Sewage greater 8
		layer GroundPollution add 1
	end

	# A NOTE ON THE SIZE OF THESE FIGURES, WHICH DECIDES WHETHER THEY WORK AT
	# ALL. A layer that decays loses a share of a cell each period, and never
	# less than one unit, so that a cell empties instead of settling just above
	# zero. A cause that writes one unit per period against a layer that takes
	# one away per period therefore produces nothing whatsoever: the file reads
	# as a working rule and the game shows an empty map. Every cause below
	# writes in threes, and the layers it writes on carry a period long enough
	# for those threes to add up.

	# Uncollected rubbish does the same, and it also breeds crime: a street
	# nobody cleans is a street nobody watches.
	layerRule TrashFoulsGround
		rate 3 hours
		layer Trash greater 15
		layer GroundPollution add 1
	end

	layerRule TrashBreedsCrime
		rate 6 hours
		layer Trash greater 20
		layer Crime add 2
	end

	# Crime grows where the land is worth nothing and where nobody is around.
	layerRule RaiseCrimeWhereValueIsLow
		rate 4 hours
		layer LandValue less 8
		layer Crime add 3
	end

	# Fire risk grows with the dirt and with the density of the buildings. The
	# rule reads Pollution because a district full of factories is the district
	# that burns.
	layerRule RaiseFireHazardWhereItIsDirty
		rate 4 hours
		layer Pollution greater 20
		layer FireHazard add 3
	end

	# Health. A clean cell recovers on its own, which is why a new city is not
	# born ill; dirt, rubbish and sewage push it back down. The three harm rules
	# are slow, so a district has the time to organise its services.
	# Recovery is slower than the harms on purpose. It used to add two an hour
	# against harms of two every six, so every cell of the map sat at capacity
	# whatever the city did to it, no district ever fell ill, and the clinics
	# had nobody to treat.
	layerRule RecoverHealth
		rate 4 hours
		layer Health add 1
	end

	layerRule PollutionHarmsHealth
		rate 4 hours
		layer Pollution greater 25
		layer Health remove 3
	end

	layerRule TrashHarmsHealth
		rate 6 hours
		layer Trash greater 15
		layer Health remove 2
	end

	layerRule GroundPollutionHarmsHealth
		rate 6 hours
		layer GroundPollution greater 20
		layer Health remove 2
	end

	# Education, skills, parks, transport, shops and access to work all fade
	# when nothing keeps them up. A school visited once is not a school.
	layerRule FadeEducation
		rate 1 day
		layer Education remove 1
	end

	layerRule FadeSkills
		rate 1 day
		layer Skills remove 1
	end

	layerRule FadeParks
		rate 1 day
		layer Parks remove 1
	end

	layerRule FadeTransitCoverage
		rate 12 hours
		layer TransitCoverage remove 1
	end

	layerRule FadeTourism
		rate 12 hours
		layer Tourism remove 1
	end

	layerRule FadeJobAccess
		rate 8 hours
		layer JobAccess remove 1
	end

	layerRule FadeShopping
		rate 8 hours
		layer Shopping remove 1
	end

	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# LAND VALUE, AS A SCALE OF THRESHOLDS
	#
	# LandValue answers one question: what is this address physically worth. It
	# is the sum of the things a surveyor would measure, and it has one rule per
	# cause, in both directions. A cause that only pushes one way is a cause the
	# city can never recover from.
	#
	# The periods differ on purpose. A cause that acts fast, such as traffic,
	# gets a short period; a cause that acts slowly, such as the ground, gets a
	# long one. This is also what keeps two rules from firing on the same tick
	# and moving the value by more than one step at a time.
	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	layerRule RaiseLandValueCleanAir
		rate 4 hours
		layer Pollution less 8
		layer LandValue add 1
	end

	layerRule DropLandValueDirtyAir
		rate 4 hours
		layer Pollution greater 20
		layer LandValue remove 1
	end

	layerRule DropLandValueFouledGround
		rate 1 day
		layer GroundPollution greater 15
		layer LandValue remove 2
	end

	layerRule RaiseLandValueQuiet
		rate 6 hours
		layer Noise less 6
		layer LandValue add 1
	end

	layerRule DropLandValueNoisy
		rate 6 hours
		layer Noise greater 20
		layer LandValue remove 1
	end

	layerRule DropLandValueCongested
		rate 3 hours
		layer Traffic greater 30
		layer LandValue remove 1
	end

	layerRule RaiseLandValueNearAPark
		rate 5 hours
		layer Parks greater 8
		layer LandValue add 1
	end

	layerRule RaiseLandValueNearTransit
		rate 5 hours
		layer TransitCoverage greater 8
		layer LandValue add 1
	end

	layerRule RaiseLandValueNearSchools
		rate 7 hours
		layer Education greater 12
		layer LandValue add 1
	end

	layerRule DropLandValueCrime
		rate 5 hours
		layer Crime greater 25
		layer LandValue remove 1
	end

	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# DESIRABILITY, THE SLOW VARIABLE
	#
	# Desirability answers a different question: would somebody want to live
	# here. It follows LandValue, but it also reads what a resident feels rather
	# than what a surveyor measures: safety and health.
	#
	# It is the slowest number in the file, and it has to be. It used to move
	# every ten ticks, half a game minute, so a district was built and abandoned
	# within the hour. Four rules, one step each, periods of six to twelve
	# hours: turning a good address into a bad one now takes days, which is a
	# speed a player can follow and act on.
	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	layerRule RaiseDesirabilityQuiet
		rate 6 hours
		layer Noise less 5
		layer Desirability add 1
	end

	layerRule RaiseDesirabilityValuable
		rate 8 hours
		layer LandValue greater 25
		layer Desirability add 1
	end

	layerRule DropDesirabilityCrime
		rate 8 hours
		layer Crime greater 25
		layer Desirability remove 1
	end

	layerRule DropDesirabilityUnhealthy
		rate 12 hours
		layer Health less 10
		layer Desirability remove 1
	end

	# =========================================================================
	# 2. THE DAY OF A HOUSE
	#
	# What shares a household between the factories and the shops is the period
	# of the rules and the number of residents, not a condition on the house:
	# one leaves for work every three quarters of an hour here, against one
	# every three hours in ShopForGoods. Sending one out every twenty minutes
	# emptied the houses long before the shops opened, and every agent the city
	# ever made was a worker.
	#
	# A period runs on the clock of its own building, from a random phase, so a
	# house grown at noon starts its commute within the hour instead of waiting
	# for the next morning.
	# =========================================================================
	buildingRule SendPeopleToWork
		rate 90 minutes
		hour between 8 18
		local People greater 0
		local People remove 1
		agent Worker to Work add [ People 1 ]
	end

	buildingRule ShopForGoods
		rate 3 hours
		hour between 10 20
		local People greater 0
		local People remove 1
		agent Shopper to Shop add [ People 1 ]
	end

	# The two rush hours. They are separate rules and not a condition inside
	# the commute, because a saturated street must not stop people from going to
	# work: it only has to cost the district its land value.
	buildingRule MorningTraffic
		rate 30 minutes
		hour between 7 9
		layer Traffic add 8
	end

	buildingRule EveningTraffic
		rate 30 minutes
		hour between 17 19
		layer Traffic add 8
	end

	# A household produces rubbish and sewage. The rubbish goes into the stock
	# of the building and needs a truck; the sewage goes straight into the
	# ground and needs a treatment plant.
	#
	# The two figures are chosen against the service that takes them away. One
	# bin an hour is exactly what a fully funded collection carries off, so a
	# city that pays in full stays clean and a city that pays half sees the
	# difference on the street. Getting this wrong is invisible in the file and
	# obvious in the Rule Log: rubbish produced more slowly than the smallest
	# truck removes leaves that truck as the only one that ever runs, and the
	# two levels above it never execute at all.
	buildingRule MakeTrash
		rate 1 hour
		local Trash add 1
	end

	buildingRule MakeSewage
		rate 1 hour
		layer Sewage add 4
	end

	# Rubbish nobody collects ends up on the street. This is what gives the
	# absence of a service a visible cost.
	buildingRule TrashPilesUp
		rate 4 hours
		local Trash greater 4
		layer Trash add 2
	end

	# Every house adds to the supply of labour. FillAJob, on the city hall,
	# is what matches this against the jobs the shops and the factories offer.
	buildingRule SupplyWorkers
		rate 4 hours
		local People greater 0
		global Workers add 1
	end

	# Residents want somewhere to shop, and they are the only ones who can say
	# so. The city hall used to read a leftover of Workers for this, which the
	# labour market empties within the hour: the appetite of the city for shops
	# fell to nothing a few days in, and no commercial zone grew again.
	buildingRule WantShops
		rate 6 hours
		local People greater 0
		global CommercialDemand add 2
	end

	# A district in poor health sends its residents to a clinic. The clinic
	# sends them home once treated, so this is a loop and not a leak.
	buildingRule SendPatient
		rate 6 hours
		layer Health less 10
		local People greater 1
		local People remove 1
		agent Patient to Clinic add [ People 1 ]
	end

	# Only the rich houses carry the two rules below, and that is the whole
	# point of wealth in this file.
	#
	# A family sends a child to the university. The university raises the
	# skills of its district and sends the graduate home. A district with
	# enough skills turns its factories into technology campuses. So a city
	# reaches high technology through its rich neighbourhoods, and only
	# through them.
	buildingRule SendStudentsToUniversity
		rate 1 day
		local People greater 2
		local People remove 1
		agent Student to University add [ People 1 ]
	end

	# A rich district also has a night life. Note the hours: 21 to 3 crosses
	# midnight, and the engine reads a range that way round as a night range.
	buildingRule GoOutAtNight
		rate 2 hours
		hour between 21 3
		local People greater 1
		local People remove 1
		agent Diner to Restaurant add [ People 1 ]
	end

	# =========================================================================
	# 3. THE DAY OF A FACTORY
	#
	# The production chain is the clearest use of onFail. A factory prefers to
	# build its goods from ore or from oil, and falls back on plain
	# labour when no mine and no well supply it. Written as three separate
	# rules, the factory with no mine would simply stop, because a rule is all
	# or nothing.
	#
	# Only the first rule of a chain is listed in "rules [ ]" on the building.
	# The engine walks the chain on its own. Two points to know:
	#
	#   Only the period of the first rule counts. The fallbacks are tried in
	#   the same pass. Give them the same "rate" so the file reads plainly,
	#   knowing that the engine does not read theirs.
	#
	#   A chain has to go one way. The parser refuses a rule that falls back on
	#   itself, but two rules that name each other would loop for ever.
	# =========================================================================
	buildingRule MakeGoodsFromOre
		rate 30 minutes
		hour between 8 18
		local People greater 0
		local Ore remove 1
		local Goods add 2
		global Money add 2
		onFail MakeGoodsFromOil
	end

	buildingRule MakeGoodsFromOil
		rate 30 minutes
		hour between 8 18
		local People greater 0
		local Oil remove 1
		local Goods add 2
		global Money add 2
		onFail MakeGoodsByHand
	end

	buildingRule MakeGoodsByHand
		rate 30 minutes
		hour between 8 18
		local People greater 0
		local Goods add 1
		global Money add 1
	end

	# Pollution and noise are separate rules on purpose. A street already as
	# dirty as it can be must not close the factory standing on it.
	# The figures are set against the diffusion and the decay of the layer, not
	# picked for their looks. A layer that carries off a sixth of itself every
	# hour settles at six times what arrives in that hour, so a factory has to
	# write in tens for a street to ever read as dirty. Write in ones and every
	# threshold above becomes a state the city cannot reach, which reads in the
	# file as a working rule and in the game as nothing at all.
	buildingRule FoulTheAir
		rate 30 minutes
		layer Pollution add 12
	end

	buildingRule FoulTheAirALittle
		rate 1 hour
		layer Pollution add 5
	end

	buildingRule MakeNoise
		rate 30 minutes
		hour between 8 18
		layer Noise add 12
	end

	buildingRule FoulTheGround
		rate 2 hours
		layer GroundPollution add 3
	end

	# The goods leave the factory on their own wheels. Without this the shops
	# never had anything to sell, and the workers looked like they were carrying
	# the stock home in the evening.
	buildingRule ShipGoodsToShop
		rate 45 minutes
		local Goods remove 1
		agent Truck to Shop add [ Goods 1 ]
	end

	# The restaurants are supplied by their own freight, and not by answering to
	# the name of a shop. A restaurant that answered to Shop as well received
	# the shoppers and the freight of the whole district, and the shops beside
	# it were never opened at all.
	buildingRule ShipGoodsToRestaurant
		rate 2 hours
		local Goods remove 1
		agent Truck to Restaurant add [ Goods 1 ]
	end

	# What the shops cannot take is sold abroad through the trade depot. This
	# is the outlet for a surplus, and the reason to build a depot at all.
	buildingRule ShipGoodsToDepot
		rate 2 hours
		local Goods remove 2
		agent Truck to Depot add [ Goods 2 ]
	end

	buildingRule SendPeopleToHome
		rate 20 minutes
		hour between 18 22
		local People remove 1
		agent People to Home add [ People 1 ]
	end

	buildingRule GoEating
		rate 30 minutes
		hour between 12 14
		local People greater 0
		local People remove 1
		agent Diner to Restaurant add [ People 1 ]
	end

	# Every workplace adds to the demand for labour, whatever it produces.
	buildingRule OfferJobs
		rate 4 hours
		global Jobs add 2
	end

	# A workplace also makes the district around it a place where work is
	# within reach, which is one of the things that raises land value.
	buildingRule OfferJobAccess
		rate 3 hours
		layer JobAccess add 12
	end

	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# Extraction. A farm, a mine and a well turn the ground into raw material,
	# and ship it to whoever accepts it.
	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	buildingRule HarvestFood
		rate 2 hours
		hour between 6 18
		local Food add 2
	end

	buildingRule ShipFoodToShop
		rate 3 hours
		local Food remove 1
		agent Truck to Shop add [ Food 1 ]
	end

	buildingRule ShipFoodToRestaurant
		rate 2 hours
		local Food remove 1
		agent Truck to Restaurant add [ Food 1 ]
	end

	buildingRule DigOre
		rate 1 hour
		hour between 6 20
		local Ore add 2
	end

	buildingRule ShipOreToFactory
		rate 90 minutes
		local Ore remove 2
		agent Truck to Work add [ Ore 2 ]
	end

	buildingRule PumpOil
		rate 1 hour
		local Oil add 2
	end

	buildingRule ShipOilToFactory
		rate 90 minutes
		local Oil remove 2
		agent Truck to Work add [ Oil 2 ]
	end

	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# The technology campus. It produces without fouling anything, and it needs
	# the skills of its district to do so. A campus in a district that lost its
	# university falls back on ordinary work, and the zone then downgrades it.
	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	buildingRule ResearchGoods
		rate 30 minutes
		hour between 8 18
		layer Skills greater 10
		local People greater 0
		local Goods add 3
		global Money add 4
		onFail MakeGoodsByHand
	end

	# =========================================================================
	# 4. THE DAY OF A SHOP
	# =========================================================================

	# A shop sells to the customers standing in it. Without the first line it
	# turned its stock into money on its own, and the shoppers were decoration.
	# This is the line that makes money follow traffic.
	buildingRule SellGoods
		rate 20 minutes
		local People greater 0
		local Goods remove 1
		global Money add 2
		local Happiness add 1
	end

	# Nobody stays where they arrived. Each building that receives people sends
	# them on: the shop back home, the restaurant back to work. Remove these
	# rules and the city accumulates residents immobile in a shop.
	buildingRule ReceiveShopper
		rate 30 minutes
		local People greater 0
		local People remove 1
		agent People to Home add [ People 1 ]
	end

	# A shop makes the district around it a place where one can buy things,
	# which is the other half of what makes an address desirable.
	buildingRule ShowShopping
		rate 3 hours
		layer Shopping add 12
	end

	# Visitors pay more than residents, and they arrive through the museums and
	# the stadiums rather than through the houses.
	buildingRule ServeTourists
		rate 1 hour
		layer Tourism greater 5
		local Goods remove 1
		global Money add 4
	end

	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# The restaurants. Three service windows, and the last one crosses
	# midnight, which is exactly what "hour between 21 3" is for.
	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# A restaurant would rather cook fresh produce, and falls back on what a
	# shop sells when no farm supplies it. Without the fallback a city with no
	# agricultural zone served nothing at all: the whole rule refuses for want
	# of one ingredient, which is precisely what a chain of rules prevents.
	buildingRule ServeLunch
		rate 15 minutes
		hour between 12 14
		local People greater 0
		local Food remove 1
		local Happiness add 1
		onFail ServeLunchFromGoods
	end

	buildingRule ServeLunchFromGoods
		rate 15 minutes
		hour between 12 14
		local People greater 0
		local Goods remove 1
		local Happiness add 1
	end

	buildingRule ServeDinner
		rate 20 minutes
		hour between 19 22
		local People greater 0
		local Food remove 1
		global Money add 2
		onFail ServeDinnerFromGoods
	end

	buildingRule ServeDinnerFromGoods
		rate 20 minutes
		hour between 19 22
		local People greater 0
		local Goods remove 1
		global Money add 2
	end

	buildingRule ServeLateNight
		rate 30 minutes
		hour between 21 3
		local People greater 0
		local Goods remove 1
		global Money add 3
		layer Noise add 4
	end

	buildingRule SendDinersBack
		rate 20 minutes
		hour between 13 15
		local People greater 0
		local People remove 1
		agent Worker to Work add [ People 1 ]
	end

	# =========================================================================
	# 5. THE BUDGET: THE TREASURY AND THE GRANTED SHARE
	#
	# This is the section to read before touching any number below.
	#
	# There are two ways for a service to fail, and a city needs to be able to
	# tell them apart.
	#
	#   The treasury is empty. "global Money" holds nothing, so nothing can be
	#   paid for at all.
	#
	#   The share granted is too small. The city is rich, and the player has
	#   given the police a tenth of what it asks for. The patrol is thin, the
	#   money stays in the bank, and crime grows anyway.
	#
	# The first is a stock and the rules move it. The second is a setting and
	# only the player moves it, through the Budget panel of the demo. A rule can
	# add and remove, never set, so no rule could hold a setting at its value.
	#
	# The graded effect comes from onFail. Each level of funding names its own
	# cost and its own effect, and the chain falls to the level the city can
	# afford:
	#
	#   PatrolFull      more than 66 percent granted, costs 3, removes 6 crime
	#   PatrolHalf      more than 33 percent granted, costs 2, removes 3 crime
	#   PatrolSkeleton  more than 0 percent granted,  costs 1, removes 1 crime
	#
	# The police station lists only PatrolFull. At a budget of zero the whole
	# chain refuses and there is no patrol at all, however full the treasury.
	#
	# Note that no level guards its cost with a condition. "remove" is already
	# a condition: it refuses unless the amount is there. So an empty treasury
	# fails the chain at the same place, and the Rule Log names the command that
	# blocked, which is what tells the two causes apart.
	#
	# WHERE THE MONEY COMES FROM. Every building pays a tax, and the rate is a
	# setting like the budget. A high rate brings more and lowers the
	# desirability of the district, so over-taxing pays for the city and empties
	# it. The city hall also receives a grant from the state, which is what lets
	# a new city start before it has anything to tax.
	# =========================================================================

	buildingRule PatrolFull
		rate 2 hours
		global PoliceBudget greater 66
		global Money remove 3
		layer Crime remove 40
		onFail PatrolHalf
	end

	buildingRule PatrolHalf
		rate 2 hours
		global PoliceBudget greater 33
		global Money remove 2
		layer Crime remove 20
		onFail PatrolSkeleton
	end

	buildingRule PatrolSkeleton
		rate 2 hours
		global PoliceBudget greater 0
		global Money remove 1
		layer Crime remove 6
	end

	buildingRule FirewatchFull
		rate 2 hours
		global FireBudget greater 66
		global Money remove 3
		layer FireHazard remove 40
		onFail FirewatchHalf
	end

	buildingRule FirewatchHalf
		rate 2 hours
		global FireBudget greater 33
		global Money remove 2
		layer FireHazard remove 20
		onFail FirewatchSkeleton
	end

	buildingRule FirewatchSkeleton
		rate 2 hours
		global FireBudget greater 0
		global Money remove 1
		layer FireHazard remove 6
	end

	buildingRule CareFull
		rate 2 hours
		global HealthBudget greater 66
		global Money remove 3
		layer Health add 6
		onFail CareHalf
	end

	buildingRule CareHalf
		rate 2 hours
		global HealthBudget greater 33
		global Money remove 2
		layer Health add 3
		onFail CareSkeleton
	end

	buildingRule CareSkeleton
		rate 2 hours
		global HealthBudget greater 0
		global Money remove 1
		layer Health add 1
	end

	buildingRule TeachFull
		rate 3 hours
		global EducationBudget greater 66
		global Money remove 3
		layer Education add 30
		onFail TeachHalf
	end

	buildingRule TeachHalf
		rate 3 hours
		global EducationBudget greater 33
		global Money remove 2
		layer Education add 15
		onFail TeachSkeleton
	end

	buildingRule TeachSkeleton
		rate 3 hours
		global EducationBudget greater 0
		global Money remove 1
		layer Education add 5
	end

	# Public transport is the levy that makes a bus stop pay for itself: it
	# covers the district and it takes cars off the street, and both raise the
	# land value through RaiseLandValueNearTransit and DropLandValueCongested.
	buildingRule RunTransitFull
		rate 1 hour
		global TransitBudget greater 66
		global Money remove 2
		layer TransitCoverage add 20
		onFail RunTransitHalf
	end

	buildingRule RunTransitHalf
		rate 1 hour
		global TransitBudget greater 33
		global Money remove 1
		layer TransitCoverage add 10
		onFail RunTransitSkeleton
	end

	buildingRule RunTransitSkeleton
		rate 1 hour
		global TransitBudget greater 0
		layer TransitCoverage add 4
	end

	buildingRule EaseTraffic
		rate 30 minutes
		layer Traffic remove 20
	end

	# Rubbish collection. The chain decides how many bins the truck removes.
	# A household produces one an hour, so the two bins of a full round match
	# that production exactly, one bin leaves half of it, and the cheapest round
	# returns some of what it collects to the street. At a budget of zero no truck leaves at
	# all, the stock of the building grows, and TrashPilesUp puts it outside.
	#
	# Note that a level asks for what it carries. A round that asked for more
	# than a household produces would refuse for want of a full load, and the
	# level below would be the only one the city ever saw.
	buildingRule CollectTrashFull
		rate 2 hours
		global WasteBudget greater 66
		global Money remove 2
		local Trash remove 2
		agent GarbageTruck to Landfill add [ Trash 2 ]
		onFail CollectTrashHalf
	end

	buildingRule CollectTrashHalf
		rate 2 hours
		global WasteBudget greater 33
		global Money remove 1
		local Trash remove 1
		agent GarbageTruck to Landfill add [ Trash 1 ]
		onFail CollectTrashSkeleton
	end

	buildingRule CollectTrashSkeleton
		rate 2 hours
		global WasteBudget greater 0
		local Trash remove 1
		layer Trash add 1
		agent GarbageTruck to Landfill add [ Trash 1 ]
	end

	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# The taxes. Same shape as the budgets, and the opposite trade: a high rate
	# brings in more money and costs the district its desirability.
	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	buildingRule PayResidentialTaxHigh
		rate 1 day
		global TaxResidential greater 12
		local People greater 0
		global Money add 6
		layer Desirability remove 1
		onFail PayResidentialTaxMedium
	end

	buildingRule PayResidentialTaxMedium
		rate 1 day
		global TaxResidential greater 6
		local People greater 0
		global Money add 4
		onFail PayResidentialTaxLow
	end

	buildingRule PayResidentialTaxLow
		rate 1 day
		global TaxResidential greater 0
		local People greater 0
		global Money add 2
	end

	buildingRule PayCommercialTaxHigh
		rate 1 day
		global TaxCommercial greater 12
		global Money add 8
		layer Desirability remove 1
		onFail PayCommercialTaxMedium
	end

	buildingRule PayCommercialTaxMedium
		rate 1 day
		global TaxCommercial greater 6
		global Money add 5
		onFail PayCommercialTaxLow
	end

	buildingRule PayCommercialTaxLow
		rate 1 day
		global TaxCommercial greater 0
		global Money add 2
	end

	buildingRule PayIndustrialTaxHigh
		rate 1 day
		global TaxIndustrial greater 12
		global Money add 10
		layer Desirability remove 1
		onFail PayIndustrialTaxMedium
	end

	buildingRule PayIndustrialTaxMedium
		rate 1 day
		global TaxIndustrial greater 6
		global Money add 6
		onFail PayIndustrialTaxLow
	end

	buildingRule PayIndustrialTaxLow
		rate 1 day
		global TaxIndustrial greater 0
		global Money add 3
	end

	# =========================================================================
	# 6. THE CITY HALL
	#
	# One building holds the accounts of the city, and a map needs exactly one.
	#
	# The three demands are what the zones spend to grow, so something has to
	# produce them and something has to consume them. A layerRule could not do
	# it: a layerRule runs on every cell of the map, so it would multiply the
	# figure by the number of cells. A single building is the right place.
	#
	# FillAJob is the trick that lets two city counters be compared, which the
	# language cannot do directly. It removes one job and one worker together, so
	# the remainder is the imbalance: a remainder of jobs means the city needs
	# residents, a remainder of workers means unemployment.
	# =========================================================================
	buildingRule StateGrant
		rate 1 day
		global Money add 400
	end

	buildingRule FillAJob
		rate 1 hour
		global Jobs remove 1
		global Workers remove 1
		global Money add 1
	end

	buildingRule VacanciesAttractResidents
		rate 2 hours
		global Jobs greater 10
		global ResidentialDemand add 4
	end

	buildingRule UnemploymentDiscouragesResidents
		rate 2 hours
		global Workers greater 10
		global ResidentialDemand remove 2
	end

	buildingRule UnemploymentBreedsCrime
		rate 4 hours
		global Workers greater 20
		layer Crime add 2
	end

	# Shops want somewhere to buy from.
	buildingRule ShopsWantFactories
		rate 4 hours
		global CommercialDemand greater 6
		global IndustrialDemand add 2
	end

	# A demand nobody spends fades, so a city that stops building stops
	# attracting. Without these three the demands would only ever grow.
	buildingRule ResidentialDemandFades
		rate 6 hours
		global ResidentialDemand remove 1
	end

	buildingRule CommercialDemandFades
		rate 6 hours
		global CommercialDemand remove 1
	end

	buildingRule IndustrialDemandFades
		rate 6 hours
		global IndustrialDemand remove 1
	end

	# =========================================================================
	# 7. UTILITIES, WASTE, LEISURE AND TRADE
	#
	# These buildings are not grown by a zone rule: they are placed by hand
	# with the Buildings tool, the way a player drops a water tower on the map.
	# Most of them only write on the ground around them, on their own clock.
	#
	# Read the numbers with the note above on how a building writes on a layer:
	# a tower supplies 400 units an hour into cells that hold 20 each, which
	# fills twenty cells an hour.
	# =========================================================================
	buildingRule SupplyWater
		rate 1 hour
		layer Water add 400
	end

	# A plant of radius five reads sixty-one cells at once, so the twelve it
	# removes is twelve over the whole district and not twelve per cell.
	buildingRule TreatSewage
		rate 1 hour
		global Money remove 1
		layer Sewage remove 12
	end

	buildingRule ProducePowerCoal
		rate 1 hour
		layer Power add 600
	end

	buildingRule ProducePowerSolar
		rate 1 hour
		hour between 7 19
		layer Power add 300
	end

	# The landfill accepts the rubbish the trucks bring, and fouls the ground
	# around itself doing so. That is the price of the cheap solution.
	buildingRule BuryTrash
		rate 1 hour
		local Trash remove 4
		global Money remove 1
	end

	# The recycling centre accepts the same rubbish, turns some of it back into
	# goods, and pays for itself. It costs more to build, in the map, than a
	# hole in the ground.
	buildingRule RecycleTrash
		rate 1 hour
		local Trash remove 3
		local Goods add 1
		global Money add 3
	end

	buildingRule OpenPark
		rate 2 hours
		layer Parks add 20
	end

	buildingRule ParkAttractsVisitors
		rate 4 hours
		layer Tourism add 8
	end

	buildingRule ShowExhibition
		rate 3 hours
		layer Tourism add 24
	end

	buildingRule HostMatch
		rate 6 hours
		hour between 15 22
		layer Tourism add 40
	end

	# The station brings visitors in, the museum entertains them, and the
	# museum then sends them to spend in a shop. Three buildings, one chain,
	# and an outlet for a city with no industry at all.
	#
	# The two rules go together. A rule that sends an agent carrying one People
	# refuses unless the building already holds one, so the station has to
	# receive its visitors from somewhere before it can send them anywhere. The
	# trains are that somewhere.
	buildingRule TrainsArrive
		rate 1 hour
		hour between 7 21
		local People add 4
	end

	buildingRule WelcomeTourists
		rate 1 hour
		hour between 8 20
		global Money remove 1
		local People remove 1
		agent Tourist to Attraction add [ People 1 ]
	end

	buildingRule EntertainTourist
		rate 30 minutes
		local People greater 0
		local People remove 1
		global Money add 4
		agent Shopper to Shop add [ People 1 ]
	end

	# The university. It consumes the student its district sent, raises the
	# skills of the whole district, counts the graduate for the city, and sends
	# the graduate home. Skills is what the industry reads to become
	# high technology.
	buildingRule GraduateStudents
		rate 6 hours
		local People greater 0
		local People remove 1
		layer Skills add 30
		global Graduates add 1
		agent People to Home add [ People 1 ]
	end

	buildingRule ResearchRaisesSkills
		rate 12 hours
		global Money remove 2
		layer Skills add 10
	end

	buildingRule TreatPatient
		rate 1 hour
		local People greater 0
		local People remove 1
		global Money remove 1
		agent People to Home add [ People 1 ]
	end

	# Trade. Importing costs money and fills the depot; exporting empties it
	# and brings money in. This is the outlet for a surplus and the answer to a
	# shortage, and it is the only rule pair in the file that trades with
	# nothing on the map.
	buildingRule ImportGoods
		rate 4 hours
		global Money remove 6
		local Goods add 3
	end

	buildingRule ExportGoods
		rate 2 hours
		local Goods remove 3
		global Money add 8
	end

	buildingRule SupplyShopsFromDepot
		rate 90 minutes
		local Goods remove 2
		agent Truck to Shop add [ Goods 2 ]
	end

	# =========================================================================
	# 8. GROWTH, WEALTH AND RUIN
	#
	# Zone rules run on the rectangle the player painted.
	#
	#   count Shack less 4              how many Shack the rectangle holds.
	#   spawn Shack at nearestSegment   build one against the closest road.
	#   upgrade Shack to House          replace one in place, keeping its stock
	#                                   and its place on the street.
	#   destroy Shack                   remove one. The emptiest one goes first.
	#
	# A zone with no road in reach grows nothing: a building needs a street to
	# stand on, or no agent could ever reach it.
	#
	# WHICH CELL A ZONE RULE READS. The plot the next building would stand on,
	# which is a cell against a road inside the rectangle. A full rectangle
	# reads its centre instead. The reach is one cell, so "layer Water greater
	# 10" means the same amount whatever the size of the rectangle.
	#
	# THE SHAPE OF EVERY ZONE BELOW. Six rules, always the same six:
	#
	#   one spawn of the poorest building, gated on the utilities and on the
	#     demand of the city, which it spends;
	#   two upgrades, poorest to middle and middle to richest, gated on the
	#     land value, on the schools, and on the absence of dirt and crime;
	#   two downgrades, the same two steps the other way, on the opposite
	#     conditions, so a district can recover instead of only decaying;
	#   one destroy, for a district nobody wants any more.
	#
	# COUNTING CAPS THE ZONE. "count" reads one type at a time, and a zone has
	# three types of building, so three count lines are what limit it. The
	# figures are the density: four of each in a low zone, six in a middle one,
	# eight in a high one.
	# =========================================================================

	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# Residential, low density: Shack, House, Villa.
	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# The period of a growth rule is how long one building takes to appear. A
	# small house goes up in two hours, a tower block in four: the taller the
	# zone, the slower and the larger each step.
	zoneRule GrowShack
		rate 2 hours
		layer Water greater 10
		layer Power greater 10
		global ResidentialDemand greater 0
		global ResidentialDemand remove 1
		count Shack less 4
		count House less 4
		count Villa less 4
		spawn Shack at nearestSegment
	end

	zoneRule UpgradeShackToHouse
		rate 1 day
		layer Desirability greater 12
		layer LandValue greater 15
		layer Education greater 8
		layer Pollution less 30
		count Shack greater 0
		upgrade Shack to House
	end

	zoneRule UpgradeHouseToVilla
		rate 1 day
		layer Desirability greater 25
		layer LandValue greater 30
		layer Education greater 20
		layer Crime less 12
		layer Pollution less 15
		count House greater 0
		upgrade House to Villa
	end

	zoneRule DowngradeVillaToHouse
		rate 1 day
		layer Desirability less 15
		count Villa greater 0
		upgrade Villa to House
	end

	zoneRule DowngradeHouseToShack
		rate 1 day
		layer Desirability less 6
		count House greater 0
		upgrade House to Shack
	end

	# The zone keeps one building whatever happens, so a district never
	# disappears completely and can come back once the air is clean again.
	zoneRule AbandonShack
		rate 1 day
		layer Desirability less 2
		count Shack greater 1
		destroy Shack
	end

	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# Residential, medium density: Tenement, Duplex, Townhouse.
	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	zoneRule GrowTenement
		rate 3 hours
		layer Water greater 10
		layer Power greater 10
		global ResidentialDemand greater 0
		global ResidentialDemand remove 1
		count Tenement less 6
		count Duplex less 6
		count Townhouse less 6
		spawn Tenement at nearestSegment
	end

	zoneRule UpgradeTenementToDuplex
		rate 1 day
		layer Desirability greater 15
		layer LandValue greater 18
		layer Education greater 10
		layer Pollution less 30
		count Tenement greater 0
		upgrade Tenement to Duplex
	end

	zoneRule UpgradeDuplexToTownhouse
		rate 1 day
		layer Desirability greater 28
		layer LandValue greater 32
		layer Education greater 22
		layer Crime less 12
		layer Pollution less 15
		count Duplex greater 0
		upgrade Duplex to Townhouse
	end

	zoneRule DowngradeTownhouseToDuplex
		rate 1 day
		layer Desirability less 18
		count Townhouse greater 0
		upgrade Townhouse to Duplex
	end

	zoneRule DowngradeDuplexToTenement
		rate 1 day
		layer Desirability less 8
		count Duplex greater 0
		upgrade Duplex to Tenement
	end

	zoneRule AbandonTenement
		rate 1 day
		layer Desirability less 2
		count Tenement greater 1
		destroy Tenement
	end

	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# Residential, high density: Projects, Apartments, Condo. A high zone asks
	# for more power than a low one, the way a tower draws more current than a
	# shack.
	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	zoneRule GrowProjects
		rate 4 hours
		layer Water greater 12
		layer Power greater 15
		layer TransitCoverage greater 4
		global ResidentialDemand greater 0
		global ResidentialDemand remove 1
		count Projects less 8
		count Apartments less 8
		count Condo less 8
		spawn Projects at nearestSegment
	end

	zoneRule UpgradeProjectsToApartments
		rate 1 day
		layer Desirability greater 18
		layer LandValue greater 22
		layer Education greater 12
		layer Crime less 20
		count Projects greater 0
		upgrade Projects to Apartments
	end

	zoneRule UpgradeApartmentsToCondo
		rate 1 day
		layer Desirability greater 30
		layer LandValue greater 35
		layer Education greater 25
		layer Crime less 10
		layer Pollution less 15
		count Apartments greater 0
		upgrade Apartments to Condo
	end

	zoneRule DowngradeCondoToApartments
		rate 1 day
		layer Desirability less 20
		count Condo greater 0
		upgrade Condo to Apartments
	end

	zoneRule DowngradeApartmentsToProjects
		rate 1 day
		layer Desirability less 10
		count Apartments greater 0
		upgrade Apartments to Projects
	end

	zoneRule AbandonProjects
		rate 1 day
		layer Desirability less 2
		count Projects greater 1
		destroy Projects
	end

	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# Commercial, low density: Bodega, Shop, Boutique. A shop reads Shopping
	# and JobAccess rather than Education: what a trader wants is customers who
	# can reach the door.
	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	zoneRule GrowBodega
		rate 3 hours
		layer Water greater 10
		layer Power greater 10
		global CommercialDemand greater 0
		global CommercialDemand remove 1
		count Bodega less 4
		count Shop less 4
		count Boutique less 4
		spawn Bodega at nearestSegment
	end

	zoneRule UpgradeBodegaToShop
		rate 1 day
		layer LandValue greater 15
		layer JobAccess greater 6
		layer Crime less 25
		count Bodega greater 0
		upgrade Bodega to Shop
	end

	zoneRule UpgradeShopToBoutique
		rate 1 day
		layer LandValue greater 30
		layer Desirability greater 22
		layer Crime less 12
		count Shop greater 0
		upgrade Shop to Boutique
	end

	zoneRule DowngradeBoutiqueToShop
		rate 1 day
		layer LandValue less 18
		count Boutique greater 0
		upgrade Boutique to Shop
	end

	zoneRule DowngradeShopToBodega
		rate 1 day
		layer LandValue less 8
		count Shop greater 0
		upgrade Shop to Bodega
	end

	zoneRule AbandonBodega
		rate 1 day
		layer LandValue less 3
		count Bodega greater 1
		destroy Bodega
	end

	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# Commercial, medium density: StripMall, Supermarket, Galleria.
	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	zoneRule GrowStripMall
		rate 4 hours
		layer Water greater 10
		layer Power greater 12
		global CommercialDemand greater 0
		global CommercialDemand remove 1
		count StripMall less 6
		count Supermarket less 6
		count Galleria less 6
		spawn StripMall at nearestSegment
	end

	zoneRule UpgradeStripMallToSupermarket
		rate 1 day
		layer LandValue greater 18
		layer JobAccess greater 8
		layer Crime less 25
		count StripMall greater 0
		upgrade StripMall to Supermarket
	end

	zoneRule UpgradeSupermarketToGalleria
		rate 1 day
		layer LandValue greater 32
		layer Desirability greater 25
		layer TransitCoverage greater 8
		count Supermarket greater 0
		upgrade Supermarket to Galleria
	end

	zoneRule DowngradeGalleriaToSupermarket
		rate 1 day
		layer LandValue less 20
		count Galleria greater 0
		upgrade Galleria to Supermarket
	end

	zoneRule DowngradeSupermarketToStripMall
		rate 1 day
		layer LandValue less 10
		count Supermarket greater 0
		upgrade Supermarket to StripMall
	end

	zoneRule AbandonStripMall
		rate 1 day
		layer LandValue less 3
		count StripMall greater 1
		destroy StripMall
	end

	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# Commercial, high density: DiscountTower, OfficeBlock, LuxuryMall. An
	# office block is where the graduates work, so this ladder reads Skills.
	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	zoneRule GrowDiscountTower
		rate 5 hours
		layer Water greater 12
		layer Power greater 15
		layer TransitCoverage greater 4
		global CommercialDemand greater 0
		global CommercialDemand remove 1
		count DiscountTower less 8
		count OfficeBlock less 8
		count LuxuryMall less 8
		spawn DiscountTower at nearestSegment
	end

	zoneRule UpgradeDiscountTowerToOfficeBlock
		rate 1 day
		layer LandValue greater 22
		layer Skills greater 8
		layer TransitCoverage greater 8
		count DiscountTower greater 0
		upgrade DiscountTower to OfficeBlock
	end

	zoneRule UpgradeOfficeBlockToLuxuryMall
		rate 1 day
		layer LandValue greater 36
		layer Desirability greater 28
		layer Skills greater 15
		count OfficeBlock greater 0
		upgrade OfficeBlock to LuxuryMall
	end

	zoneRule DowngradeLuxuryMallToOfficeBlock
		rate 1 day
		layer LandValue less 24
		count LuxuryMall greater 0
		upgrade LuxuryMall to OfficeBlock
	end

	zoneRule DowngradeOfficeBlockToDiscountTower
		rate 1 day
		layer LandValue less 12
		count OfficeBlock greater 0
		upgrade OfficeBlock to DiscountTower
	end

	zoneRule AbandonDiscountTower
		rate 1 day
		layer LandValue less 3
		count DiscountTower greater 1
		destroy DiscountTower
	end

	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# The farms. One type, no ladder: a farm is a farm. It asks for water and
	# for clean ground, and it refuses to grow next to a factory.
	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	zoneRule GrowFarm
		rate 6 hours
		layer Water greater 15
		layer GroundPollution less 10
		global IndustrialDemand greater 0
		global IndustrialDemand remove 1
		count Farm less 6
		spawn Farm at nearestSegment
	end

	zoneRule AbandonFarm
		rate 1 day
		layer GroundPollution greater 40
		count Farm greater 1
		destroy Farm
	end

	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# The industry, and the loop this whole file was built for.
	#
	# FactoryDirty is what a city can afford at the start: it produces and it
	# fouls. FactoryClean asks for an educated workforce. TechCampus asks for
	# skills, and skills come from a university, and a university is fed by the
	# students of the rich houses. So the road to high technology runs through
	# the rich neighbourhoods, and there is no other road.
	#
	# The last rule also spends Graduates, so a single graduation cannot
	# convert the whole industrial belt.
	# -------------------------------------------------------------------------
	# A cell of the power layer holds twenty, and a condition is strict, so
	# asking for more than twenty asks for something no cell can hold: the zone
	# would never grow at all. Sixteen is a heavy draw and is reachable.
	zoneRule GrowFactory
		rate 4 hours
		layer Water greater 10
		layer Power greater 16
		global IndustrialDemand greater 0
		global IndustrialDemand remove 1
		count FactoryDirty less 6
		count FactoryClean less 6
		count TechCampus less 6
		spawn FactoryDirty at nearestSegment
	end

	zoneRule IndustryGetsCleaner
		rate 1 day
		layer Education greater 15
		layer Power greater 16
		count FactoryDirty greater 0
		upgrade FactoryDirty to FactoryClean
	end

	zoneRule IndustryGoesHighTech
		rate 1 day
		layer Skills greater 20
		layer Pollution less 20
		global Graduates greater 3
		global Graduates remove 4
		count FactoryClean greater 0
		upgrade FactoryClean to TechCampus
	end

	zoneRule HighTechLeavesForLackOfSkills
		rate 1 day
		layer Skills less 6
		count TechCampus greater 0
		upgrade TechCampus to FactoryClean
	end

	zoneRule IndustryGetsDirtierAgain
		rate 1 day
		layer Education less 5
		count FactoryClean greater 0
		upgrade FactoryClean to FactoryDirty
	end

	zoneRule AbandonFactory
		rate 1 day
		layer Power less 3
		count FactoryDirty greater 1
		destroy FactoryDirty
	end
end


# =============================================================================
# BUILDINGS - every kind of building, and what each one is able to do.
#
# One line per kind. The parts of a line:
#
#   layerRadius 3      how far, in cells, its rules read and write the ground.
#                      The shape is a diamond around the building. A radius of
#                      1 is the cell itself and its four neighbours.
#
#   rules [ ... ]      the rules it runs. A rule missing from this list never
#                      runs on this building, however well it is written. Only
#                      the first rule of an onFail chain belongs here.
#
#   targets [ Home ]   the names agents look for. "agent Worker to Home" ends
#                      its trip in a building whose targets hold "Home". A
#                      building can answer to several names, and a building
#                      with no target never receives anything.
#
#   caps [ People 8 ]  how much it can hold. An agent carrying one more People
#                      to a full house is refused and keeps looking. A resource
#                      absent from the caps is a resource the building cannot
#                      hold at all, and an upgrade to it drops that stock.
#
#   resources [ ... ]  what it holds when it is built.
#
# THE NINE HOUSES AND THE NINE SHOPS. Read them as a table. Down the page, the
# density the zone paints: small, middle, tall. Across each group of three, the
# wealth an upgrade brings: poor, ordinary, rich. A tall poor building holds
# more people than a small rich one, and is worth far less.
#
# All nine houses answer to "Home", so a worker sent home at six in the evening
# reaches whichever house is nearest, whatever it is called. The three rich ones
# also answer to "HomeRich", which is the name a rule would use to reach only
# them. All nine shops answer to "Shop" for the same reason.
# =============================================================================
buildings

	# --- Residential, low density -------------------------------------------
	building Shack color 0x8B6F5A layerRadius 1 rules [ SendPeopleToWork ShopForGoods MorningTraffic EveningTraffic MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp SupplyWorkers WantShops SendPatient PayResidentialTaxHigh ] targets [ Home ] caps [ People 6 Trash 10 Happiness 5 ] resources [ People 5 ]
	building House color 0xFF00FF layerRadius 1 rules [ SendPeopleToWork ShopForGoods MorningTraffic EveningTraffic MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp SupplyWorkers WantShops SendPatient PayResidentialTaxHigh ] targets [ Home ] caps [ People 8 Trash 12 Happiness 10 ] resources [ People 8 ]
	building Villa color 0xFF99EE layerRadius 2 rules [ SendPeopleToWork ShopForGoods MorningTraffic EveningTraffic MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp SupplyWorkers WantShops SendPatient PayResidentialTaxHigh SendStudentsToUniversity GoOutAtNight ] targets [ Home HomeRich ] caps [ People 6 Trash 12 Happiness 20 ] resources [ People 5 ]

	# --- Residential, medium density ----------------------------------------
	building Tenement color 0x7A6A55 layerRadius 1 rules [ SendPeopleToWork ShopForGoods MorningTraffic EveningTraffic MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp SupplyWorkers WantShops SendPatient PayResidentialTaxHigh ] targets [ Home ] caps [ People 10 Trash 16 Happiness 5 ] resources [ People 8 ]
	building Duplex color 0xCC66AA layerRadius 1 rules [ SendPeopleToWork ShopForGoods MorningTraffic EveningTraffic MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp SupplyWorkers WantShops SendPatient PayResidentialTaxHigh ] targets [ Home ] caps [ People 16 Trash 20 Happiness 12 ] resources [ People 12 ]
	building Townhouse color 0xEE88DD layerRadius 2 rules [ SendPeopleToWork ShopForGoods MorningTraffic EveningTraffic MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp SupplyWorkers WantShops SendPatient PayResidentialTaxHigh SendStudentsToUniversity GoOutAtNight ] targets [ Home HomeRich ] caps [ People 14 Trash 20 Happiness 24 ] resources [ People 10 ]

	# --- Residential, high density ------------------------------------------
	building Projects color 0x66605A layerRadius 2 rules [ SendPeopleToWork ShopForGoods MorningTraffic EveningTraffic MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp SupplyWorkers WantShops SendPatient PayResidentialTaxHigh ] targets [ Home ] caps [ People 24 Trash 30 Happiness 5 ] resources [ People 20 ]
	building Apartments color 0xAA5599 layerRadius 2 rules [ SendPeopleToWork ShopForGoods MorningTraffic EveningTraffic MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp SupplyWorkers WantShops SendPatient PayResidentialTaxHigh ] targets [ Home ] caps [ People 36 Trash 36 Happiness 15 ] resources [ People 28 ]
	building Condo color 0xDD77EE layerRadius 2 rules [ SendPeopleToWork ShopForGoods MorningTraffic EveningTraffic MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp SupplyWorkers WantShops SendPatient PayResidentialTaxHigh SendStudentsToUniversity GoOutAtNight ] targets [ Home HomeRich ] caps [ People 30 Trash 30 Happiness 30 ] resources [ People 24 ]

	# --- Commercial, low density --------------------------------------------
	building Bodega color 0xBB8844 layerRadius 1 rules [ SellGoods ReceiveShopper ShowShopping ServeTourists MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp OfferJobs OfferJobAccess PayCommercialTaxHigh ] targets [ Shop ] caps [ People 4 Goods 12 Food 8 Trash 10 Happiness 8 ] resources [ ]
	building Shop color 0xFFAA00 layerRadius 2 rules [ SellGoods ReceiveShopper ShowShopping ServeTourists MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp OfferJobs OfferJobAccess PayCommercialTaxHigh ] targets [ Shop ] caps [ People 6 Goods 30 Food 20 Trash 14 Happiness 20 ] resources [ ]
	building Boutique color 0xFFCC66 layerRadius 1 rules [ SellGoods ReceiveShopper ShowShopping ServeTourists MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp OfferJobs OfferJobAccess PayCommercialTaxHigh ] targets [ Shop ] caps [ People 6 Goods 20 Food 12 Trash 10 Happiness 30 ] resources [ ]

	# --- Commercial, medium density -----------------------------------------
	building StripMall color 0xAA7733 layerRadius 2 rules [ SellGoods ReceiveShopper ShowShopping ServeTourists MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp OfferJobs OfferJobAccess PayCommercialTaxHigh ] targets [ Shop ] caps [ People 10 Goods 40 Food 24 Trash 20 Happiness 12 ] resources [ ]
	building Supermarket color 0xFF9933 layerRadius 2 rules [ SellGoods ReceiveShopper ShowShopping ServeTourists MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp OfferJobs OfferJobAccess PayCommercialTaxHigh ] targets [ Shop ] caps [ People 16 Goods 80 Food 50 Trash 26 Happiness 24 ] resources [ ]
	building Galleria color 0xFFBB55 layerRadius 2 rules [ SellGoods ReceiveShopper ShowShopping ServeTourists MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp OfferJobs OfferJobAccess PayCommercialTaxHigh ] targets [ Shop ] caps [ People 20 Goods 70 Food 40 Trash 24 Happiness 40 ] resources [ ]

	# --- Commercial, high density -------------------------------------------
	building DiscountTower color 0x8C6A2F layerRadius 2 rules [ SellGoods ReceiveShopper ShowShopping ServeTourists MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp OfferJobs OfferJobAccess PayCommercialTaxHigh ] targets [ Shop ] caps [ People 20 Goods 90 Food 40 Trash 30 Happiness 10 ] resources [ ]
	building OfficeBlock color 0x557799 layerRadius 2 rules [ SellGoods ReceiveShopper ShowShopping ServeTourists MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp OfferJobs OfferJobAccess PayCommercialTaxHigh ] targets [ Shop ] caps [ People 40 Goods 60 Food 30 Trash 30 Happiness 20 ] resources [ ]
	building LuxuryMall color 0xFFDD88 layerRadius 3 rules [ SellGoods ReceiveShopper ShowShopping ServeTourists MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull TrashPilesUp OfferJobs OfferJobAccess PayCommercialTaxHigh ] targets [ Shop ] caps [ People 30 Goods 120 Food 60 Trash 30 Happiness 50 ] resources [ ]

	# --- Food service, placed by hand ---------------------------------------
	# The restaurant answers to its own name only. Answering to Shop as well is
	# how the freight and the shoppers ended up at the canteen and the shops
	# were never opened.
	building Restaurant color 0xFF6644 layerRadius 1 rules [ ServeLunch ServeDinner ServeLateNight SendDinersBack MakeTrash MakeSewage CollectTrashFull OfferJobs OfferJobAccess PayCommercialTaxHigh ] targets [ Restaurant ] caps [ People 10 Goods 20 Food 24 Trash 12 Happiness 20 ] resources [ ]

	# --- Extraction and industry --------------------------------------------
	# All four answer to "Work", so a worker leaving home reaches whichever is
	# nearest. A truck carrying ore also asks for "Work", and only a building
	# with room for ore accepts it: the load decides, not the name.
	building Farm color 0x88AA44 layerRadius 3 rules [ HarvestFood ShipFoodToShop ShipFoodToRestaurant SendPeopleToHome OfferJobs OfferJobAccess PayIndustrialTaxHigh ] targets [ Work ] caps [ People 8 Food 40 ] resources [ ]
	building FactoryDirty color 0x00AAFF layerRadius 3 rules [ MakeGoodsFromOre FoulTheAir MakeNoise ShipGoodsToShop ShipGoodsToRestaurant ShipGoodsToDepot SendPeopleToHome GoEating OfferJobs OfferJobAccess MakeTrash CollectTrashFull PayIndustrialTaxHigh ] targets [ Work ] caps [ People 12 Goods 30 Ore 20 Oil 20 Trash 20 ] resources [ ]
	building FactoryClean color 0x00DDCC layerRadius 3 rules [ MakeGoodsFromOre FoulTheAirALittle ShipGoodsToShop ShipGoodsToRestaurant ShipGoodsToDepot SendPeopleToHome GoEating OfferJobs OfferJobAccess MakeTrash CollectTrashFull PayIndustrialTaxHigh ] targets [ Work ] caps [ People 16 Goods 40 Ore 24 Oil 24 Trash 20 ] resources [ ]
	building TechCampus color 0x66FFCC layerRadius 3 rules [ ResearchGoods ShipGoodsToShop ShipGoodsToDepot SendPeopleToHome GoEating OfferJobs OfferJobAccess MakeTrash CollectTrashFull PayIndustrialTaxHigh ] targets [ Work ] caps [ People 24 Goods 60 Ore 10 Oil 10 Trash 16 ] resources [ ]

	building OreMine color 0x776655 layerRadius 3 rules [ DigOre ShipOreToFactory FoulTheGround SendPeopleToHome OfferJobs PayIndustrialTaxHigh ] targets [ Work ] caps [ People 10 Ore 40 ] resources [ ]
	building OilWell color 0x332211 layerRadius 3 rules [ PumpOil ShipOilToFactory FoulTheGround FoulTheAirALittle SendPeopleToHome OfferJobs PayIndustrialTaxHigh ] targets [ Work ] caps [ People 6 Oil 40 ] resources [ ]

	# --- Utilities ----------------------------------------------------------
	# No target: nothing is ever sent to a water tower, so it never needs to
	# accept an agent. No stock either: it only writes on the layers around it.
	building WaterTower color 0x3399FF layerRadius 4 rules [ SupplyWater ] targets [ ] caps [ ] resources [ ]
	building WaterTreatment color 0x336655 layerRadius 5 rules [ TreatSewage ] targets [ ] caps [ ] resources [ ]
	building CoalPlant color 0xFFCC00 layerRadius 6 rules [ ProducePowerCoal FoulTheAir MakeNoise ] targets [ ] caps [ ] resources [ ]
	building SolarPlant color 0xFFEE88 layerRadius 5 rules [ ProducePowerSolar ] targets [ ] caps [ ] resources [ ]

	# --- Waste --------------------------------------------------------------
	# Both accept the rubbish trucks, under the same name "Landfill", so a
	# truck takes whichever is nearer. The hole in the ground fouls the soil;
	# the recycling centre turns rubbish back into goods and pays for itself.
	building Landfill color 0x665544 layerRadius 4 rules [ BuryTrash FoulTheGround ] targets [ Landfill ] caps [ Trash 200 ] resources [ ]
	building RecyclingCenter color 0x44AA77 layerRadius 2 rules [ RecycleTrash SupplyShopsFromDepot ] targets [ Landfill ] caps [ Trash 120 Goods 40 ] resources [ ]

	# --- Safety -------------------------------------------------------------
	# Each lists only the first rule of its funding chain. See the budget.
	building PoliceStation color 0x3355DD layerRadius 4 rules [ PatrolFull ] targets [ ] caps [ ] resources [ ]
	building FireStation color 0xDD2222 layerRadius 4 rules [ FirewatchFull ] targets [ ] caps [ ] resources [ ]

	# --- Education ----------------------------------------------------------
	# The school and the high school run the same funding chain and differ by
	# their reach: a high school serves a wider district than a primary school.
	# The university is the only one that receives an agent, and the only one
	# that raises Skills.
	building School color 0x22BBBB layerRadius 3 rules [ TeachFull ] targets [ ] caps [ ] resources [ ]
	building HighSchool color 0x1199AA layerRadius 5 rules [ TeachFull ] targets [ ] caps [ ] resources [ ]
	building University color 0x0077AA layerRadius 6 rules [ TeachFull GraduateStudents ResearchRaisesSkills ] targets [ University ] caps [ People 40 ] resources [ ]

	# --- Health -------------------------------------------------------------
	# Both answer to "Clinic", so a patient goes to whichever is nearer.
	building Clinic color 0xFF99AA layerRadius 3 rules [ CareFull TreatPatient ] targets [ Clinic ] caps [ People 20 ] resources [ ]
	building Hospital color 0xFF6688 layerRadius 6 rules [ CareFull TreatPatient ] targets [ Clinic ] caps [ People 60 ] resources [ ]

	# --- Leisure and tourism ------------------------------------------------
	# The museum and the stadium answer to "Attraction", which is the name the
	# station sends its visitors to. Both then send the visitor to spend in a
	# shop, so tourism is a chain of three buildings and not a bonus.
	building Park color 0x33CC55 layerRadius 3 rules [ OpenPark ParkAttractsVisitors ] targets [ ] caps [ ] resources [ ]
	building Museum color 0xCC66FF layerRadius 4 rules [ ShowExhibition EntertainTourist ] targets [ Attraction ] caps [ People 30 ] resources [ ]
	building Stadium color 0xFF66FF layerRadius 5 rules [ HostMatch EntertainTourist MakeNoise ] targets [ Attraction ] caps [ People 80 ] resources [ ]

	# --- Transport ----------------------------------------------------------
	building BusStop color 0x44AAFF layerRadius 3 rules [ RunTransitFull EaseTraffic ] targets [ ] caps [ ] resources [ ]
	building MetroStation color 0x2266CC layerRadius 6 rules [ RunTransitFull EaseTraffic ] targets [ ] caps [ ] resources [ ]
	building TrainStation color 0x8899AA layerRadius 4 rules [ RunTransitFull TrainsArrive WelcomeTourists ] targets [ ] caps [ People 40 ] resources [ People 8 ]

	# --- Trade --------------------------------------------------------------
	building TradeDepot color 0x998877 layerRadius 2 rules [ ImportGoods ExportGoods SupplyShopsFromDepot ShipGoodsToRestaurant ] targets [ Depot ] caps [ Goods 120 Ore 60 Oil 60 Food 60 ] resources [ ]

	# --- The city hall ------------------------------------------------------
	# A map needs exactly one. It holds the accounts of the city: the state
	# grant, the labour market, and the three demands the zones spend to grow.
	building CityHall color 0xEEEEDD layerRadius 4 rules [ StateGrant FillAJob VacanciesAttractResidents UnemploymentDiscouragesResidents UnemploymentBreedsCrime ShopsWantFactories ResidentialDemandFades CommercialDemandFades IndustrialDemandFades ] targets [ ] caps [ ] resources [ ]
end


# =============================================================================
# LAYERS - the ground under the city.
#
# A layer is one number per cell of the map, over the whole world. The demo
# draws each one as a heatmap in the colour given here, and a cell at capacity
# is a cell drawn full.
#
#   capacity      the most one cell can hold. It is also the size of one cell
#                 when a building writes: see the note at the top of the rules.
#
#   diffusion     the share of a cell, in percent, that moves to its four
#                 neighbours each period. The four share it equally and the
#                 remainder stays, so diffusion moves an amount and never
#                 creates or loses one.
#
#   decay         the share of a cell, in percent, that disappears each period.
#                 A layer that loses always loses at least one unit, so a cell
#                 does empty in the end instead of settling just above zero.
#
#   rate          the period of diffusion and decay. Not the period of the
#                 rules: each rule carries its own.
#
# WHY DIFFUSION AND DECAY ARE NOT RULES. A layer rule reads and writes the one
# cell it stands on, so no rule can move an amount to the cell next door. The
# file used to fake it with a pair of rules, one adding one and one removing
# one, which faded pollution evenly over the whole map and never carried the
# smoke of a factory to the street beside it.
#
# READ THE THREE FAMILIES BELOW AS THREE SPEEDS. Noise travels far and stops the
# moment the lorry has passed. Smoke travels and fades within the hour. What is
# in the soil hardly moves and hardly leaves.
# =============================================================================
layers

	# --- The networks. A cell holds twenty, and a tower supplies four hundred
	# an hour, which fills twenty cells. Both lose pressure, so a utility has
	# to keep running instead of electrifying the city once and for all.
	layer Water color 0x0000FF capacity 20 decay 10 rate 2 hours rules [ ]
	layer Power color 0xFFFF66 capacity 20 decay 10 rate 2 hours rules [ ]
	layer Grass color 0x00FF00 capacity 10 rules [ CreateGrass ]

	# --- What the buildings foul. Sewage seeps, smoke flies, soil keeps.
	#
	# A rule belongs to one layer and no more. Listing PollutionHarmsHealth
	# under Pollution and under Health would run it twice a period and halve
	# the health of the city at twice the speed the numbers say.
	layer Sewage color 0x6B8E23 capacity 40 diffusion 8 decay 4 rate 2 hours rules [ SewageFoulsGround ]
	layer Trash color 0x886644 capacity 40 decay 2 rate 6 hours rules [ TrashFoulsGround TrashBreedsCrime ]
	layer Pollution color 0x555555 capacity 80 diffusion 14 decay 6 rate 1 hour rules [ ]
	layer GroundPollution color 0x7B5B3A capacity 80 diffusion 4 decay 1 rate 1 day rules [ ]
	layer Noise color 0x999999 capacity 60 diffusion 30 decay 14 rate 1 hour rules [ ]
	layer Traffic color 0xFF4444 capacity 60 diffusion 16 decay 14 rate 2 hours rules [ ]

	# --- What people fear and what burns. Both spread a little, because a bad
	# street makes the next one worse, and both fade when a service works.
	layer Crime color 0xCC2222 capacity 60 diffusion 12 decay 5 rate 6 hours rules [ RaiseCrimeWhereValueIsLow ]
	layer FireHazard color 0xFF8800 capacity 60 diffusion 6 decay 5 rate 6 hours rules [ RaiseFireHazardWhereItIsDirty ]

	# --- What the services give. Diffusion is what turns the thirty units a
	# school writes into a district that is schooled, rather than one bright
	# cell in the middle of nothing.
	layer Education color 0x66CCFF capacity 50 diffusion 20 rate 3 hours rules [ FadeEducation ]
	layer Skills color 0x00CC88 capacity 50 diffusion 16 rate 6 hours rules [ FadeSkills ]
	layer Health color 0xFF99AA capacity 50 diffusion 20 rate 2 hours rules [ RecoverHealth PollutionHarmsHealth TrashHarmsHealth GroundPollutionHarmsHealth ]
	layer TransitCoverage color 0x44AAFF capacity 40 diffusion 24 rate 2 hours rules [ FadeTransitCoverage ]
	layer Parks color 0x33CC55 capacity 30 diffusion 24 rate 4 hours rules [ FadeParks ]
	layer Tourism color 0xFF66FF capacity 40 diffusion 20 rate 4 hours rules [ FadeTourism ]
	layer JobAccess color 0x8844FF capacity 40 diffusion 24 rate 3 hours rules [ FadeJobAccess ]
	layer Shopping color 0xFFCC88 capacity 40 diffusion 24 rate 3 hours rules [ FadeShopping ]

	# --- The two that decide the game. LandValue is what a surveyor measures,
	# Desirability is what a resident feels. Both spread to the street next
	# door, and neither decays: only a rule moves them, which is what makes
	# them the slow variables of the city.
	layer LandValue color 0xCCAA00 capacity 50 diffusion 12 rate 6 hours rules [ RaiseLandValueCleanAir DropLandValueDirtyAir DropLandValueFouledGround RaiseLandValueQuiet DropLandValueNoisy DropLandValueCongested RaiseLandValueNearAPark RaiseLandValueNearTransit RaiseLandValueNearSchools DropLandValueCrime ]
	layer Desirability color 0x88FF88 capacity 50 diffusion 10 rate 6 hours rules [ RaiseDesirabilityQuiet RaiseDesirabilityValuable DropDesirabilityCrime DropDesirabilityUnhealthy ]
end


# =============================================================================
# ZONES - what the player paints on the map.
#
# A zone holds no building of its own. It is a rectangle plus a list of rules,
# and those rules are what build, improve, ruin and remove things inside it.
# This is the game itself: paint a zone next to a road, supply it with water and
# power, and observe what the ground around it produces.
#
# EIGHT ZONES, AND WHAT CHOOSING ONE MEANS. The three residential zones and the
# three commercial ones differ only by density: the same wealth ladder runs
# inside each, but a high zone grows taller buildings and asks for more power
# and for public transport before it grows anything at all. Painting high
# density on the edge of the map with no bus stop grows nothing, which is the
# lesson.
#
# The farms and the industry have no density: a farm is a farm, and the
# industrial ladder is a ladder of technology rather than of wealth.
# =============================================================================
zones
	zone ResidentialLow color 0x66CC66 rules [ GrowShack UpgradeShackToHouse UpgradeHouseToVilla DowngradeVillaToHouse DowngradeHouseToShack AbandonShack ]
	zone ResidentialMedium color 0x44AA44 rules [ GrowTenement UpgradeTenementToDuplex UpgradeDuplexToTownhouse DowngradeTownhouseToDuplex DowngradeDuplexToTenement AbandonTenement ]
	zone ResidentialHigh color 0x228822 rules [ GrowProjects UpgradeProjectsToApartments UpgradeApartmentsToCondo DowngradeCondoToApartments DowngradeApartmentsToProjects AbandonProjects ]

	zone CommercialLow color 0xEECC66 rules [ GrowBodega UpgradeBodegaToShop UpgradeShopToBoutique DowngradeBoutiqueToShop DowngradeShopToBodega AbandonBodega ]
	zone CommercialMedium color 0xDDAA44 rules [ GrowStripMall UpgradeStripMallToSupermarket UpgradeSupermarketToGalleria DowngradeGalleriaToSupermarket DowngradeSupermarketToStripMall AbandonStripMall ]
	zone CommercialHigh color 0xBB8822 rules [ GrowDiscountTower UpgradeDiscountTowerToOfficeBlock UpgradeOfficeBlockToLuxuryMall DowngradeLuxuryMallToOfficeBlock DowngradeOfficeBlockToDiscountTower AbandonDiscountTower ]

	zone Agricultural color 0xAACC66 rules [ GrowFarm AbandonFarm ]
	zone Industrial color 0xAA6644 rules [ GrowFactory IndustryGetsCleaner IndustryGoesHighTech HighTechLeavesForLackOfSkills IndustryGetsDirtierAgain AbandonFactory ]
end
